:: F1 {"position":"275,25","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: b) Pancreas

The pancreas contains beta cells in the islets of Langerhans that detect rising blood glucose and secrete insulin. Insulin coordinates whole body glucose uptake and storage. The liver responds to insulin but does not release it. Adrenal glands produce hormones such as adrenaline and cortisol, while kidneys regulate filtration and excretion. This endocrine control is central to metabolic homeostasis and postprandial glucose regulation.

