:: F10 {"position":"25,275","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: c) Enzyme → signalling pathway → cell → organ → whole organism

Metabolic regulation operates across hierarchical levels. Enzyme activity influences signalling pathways, which affect cellular behaviour. Coordinated responses across cells contribute to organ function and ultimately whole organism physiology. The alternative sequences do not represent increasing biological scale or regulatory organisation. This hierarchy illustrates how molecular events propagate to systemic metabolic control.

