:: F4 {"position":"1025,25","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: c) Transport of glucose transporters to the cell membrane

Insulin stimulates signalling pathways that increase the movement of glucose transporters, especially GLUT4, to the plasma membrane in responsive tissues. This enhances glucose uptake from the circulation. Insulin generally promotes glycogen synthesis rather than glycogen breakdown, suppresses glucose release, and inhibits ketone body production. These actions help reduce blood glucose after feeding and support energy storage.

