:: F6 {"position":"275,150","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: c) Maintaining blood glucose levels

During short-term fasting, the liver maintains blood glucose through glycogenolysis and increasingly through gluconeogenesis. This preserves glucose supply for tissues with high glucose requirements. Ketone production becomes more prominent during prolonged fasting. Cholesterol synthesis and fat storage are not the primary priorities during this period. Hepatic regulation is crucial for maintaining systemic energy balance between meals.

