:: F7 {"position":"525,150","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: d) cAMP

cAMP is a classic second messenger generated from ATP by adenylyl cyclase. It transmits extracellular hormonal signals to intracellular targets, often through protein kinase A. Glycogen is a storage polysaccharide, DNA stores genetic information, and ATP serves mainly as an energy carrier and precursor. Second messenger systems allow amplification and regulation of metabolic signalling pathways.

