:: F8 {"position":"775,150","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: b) Insulin

Pre-diabetes is characterised by reduced cellular responsiveness to insulin, a condition known as insulin resistance. As insulin signalling becomes less effective, glucose uptake and metabolic regulation are impaired. Glucagon has distinct physiological roles, while lactate and glycogen are metabolites rather than the primary signalling defect. Persistent insulin resistance increases the risk of progression to type 2 diabetes and associated metabolic disorders.

