:: F9 {"position":"1025,150","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: c) The product of energy-generating metabolism

ATP reflects the cellular energy state and can act as a feedback signal when energy supplies are sufficient. By inhibiting components of energy-generating pathways, ATP helps match production with demand. ATP is not an oxygen substrate and is not a membrane receptor. This feedback regulation contributes to efficient control of oxidative phosphorylation and broader metabolic homeostasis.

